WEBVTT

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:41.390
Take care!

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:48.850
On this day, Marilla hands all the
chores at home over to Anne

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:52.310
and sets off from Green Gables
early in the morning.

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:56.870
She's leaving for Charlottetown with
Dr. Spencer's referral letter.

00:01:58.290 --> 00:02:02.440
She intends to go there to get examined
by the famous eye specialist that is visiting.

00:02:03.830 --> 00:02:09.160
After noon, the coach driven by Martin
arrives at the hospital.

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:22.270
We're hardly ever in town. Settle the horse
and shop around nearby if you wish to.

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:25.010
Looks like it will take quite some time.

00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:25.830
Yes.

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:38.820
Excuse me. I've been referred by
Dr Spencer from Avonlea.

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:41.730
Let me see. Miss Marilla Cuthbert?

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:43.600
Please sit down over there for a while.

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:18.080
Please come in.

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:20.710
Oh! Diana!

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:22.820
I'm relieved to see that look of yours.

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:25.130
What happened to you yesterday, Anne?

00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:29.130
I'm sorry. I suddenly thought of Matthew...

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:33.130
I thought it was something like that.
I've come back to invite you again today.

00:03:33.630 --> 00:03:36.200
It's about time you started thinking about your future.

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:37.770
Thank you, Diana.

00:03:37.810 --> 00:03:41.540
And so, I have to learn not to burn bread
so I won't go hungry in the future.

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:43.230
Eh? Where's Marilla?

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:45.650
She's gone out today.

00:03:46.990 --> 00:03:50.980
Can you bring in the laundry for me?
It has to be ironed as well.

00:03:51.220 --> 00:03:53.290
Well... All right!

00:03:53.380 --> 00:03:56.730
If you promise you won't behave
like you did yesterday, I'll help you.

00:03:57.400 --> 00:04:01.030
When you've finished you're chores,
please come to my house to see the sewing machine.

00:04:01.070 --> 00:04:02.990
Oh! I'm so happy, Diana.

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:33.360
Oh...

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:56.520
So, how is it, Doctor?

00:04:58.490 --> 00:05:02.690
The symptoms have advanced quite a lot.
But it shouldn't be too late.

00:05:03.830 --> 00:05:05.110
Too late?

00:05:15.700 --> 00:05:17.040
How did it go?

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:57.010
Well, are you going back already, Anne?

00:05:57.050 --> 00:05:58.580
Sorry to have troubled you.

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:00.660
Since Marilla had to go out...

00:06:01.670 --> 00:06:06.460
By the way, Anne. There's something I
hope you would consider.

00:06:06.950 --> 00:06:10.960
Actually, I'm thinking of renting the Cuthbert family's field.

00:06:11.740 --> 00:06:12.660
The field?

00:06:12.700 --> 00:06:20.200
Yes, I just bought a new machine, and intend
to grow more potatoes next year.

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:22.700
Green Gables must be
having a difficult time

00:06:22.710 --> 00:06:24.620
because of what happened
to Abbey Bank, right?

00:06:24.910 --> 00:06:28.440
My terms won't be too bad.

00:06:28.480 --> 00:06:35.150
But Matthew just passed away. It didn't
seem appropriate to bring it up.

00:06:35.190 --> 00:06:38.570
Can you help me ask Marilla about it?

00:06:40.230 --> 00:06:45.790
Just bring it up when there's a chance.
It'll be for next year anyway.

00:07:01.030 --> 00:07:02.710
- Martin.
- Yes.

00:07:02.750 --> 00:07:05.190
Take me to Mrs. Lynde's house first.

00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:05.780
Yes.

00:07:07.300 --> 00:07:08.670
You must be tired.

00:07:09.070 --> 00:07:12.310
Go back ahead of me and
tell Anne that I will be late.

00:07:12.390 --> 00:07:14.360
- But...
- It's all right.

00:07:15.230 --> 00:07:16.160
Very well.

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:23.200
I see. That's good.

00:07:23.850 --> 00:07:28.020
It seems it was worth
the bother to go to town.

00:07:28.110 --> 00:07:29.960
Well, that may be so.

00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:34.270
What's the matter, Marilla?
Cheer up.

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:35.140
Yes.

00:07:36.280 --> 00:07:42.400
Actually, since Matthew died,
there's something I've kept thinking about.

00:07:42.490 --> 00:07:44.110
What do you think, Marilla?

00:07:44.250 --> 00:07:49.600
This is a chance to sell Green Gables.
Why don't you settle down in a boarding house?

00:07:49.760 --> 00:07:50.910
Rachel!

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:52.720
Though it may seem drastic,

00:07:53.320 --> 00:07:57.450
Abbey Bank's bankruptcy must have
been a great blow to you.

00:07:57.540 --> 00:08:01.590
Anne will leave for Redmond after
the summer vacation.

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:05.720
I think it's for the best.
As for the buyer, I can...

00:08:05.810 --> 00:08:07.480
I can't do it, Rachel.

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:12.100
There's no way I can sell Green Gables.

00:08:12.190 --> 00:08:13.990
Besides, Matthew wouldn't have agreed.

00:08:16.290 --> 00:08:19.410
I must have shocked you with the idea.

00:08:19.770 --> 00:08:22.790
I think you should take
some time to think about it.

00:08:38.550 --> 00:08:40.230
Welcome back, Marilla.

00:08:40.320 --> 00:08:41.420
I'm back...

00:08:41.850 --> 00:08:44.410
You must be hungry.
Tea will be ready soon.

00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:54.420
You look really tired, Marilla.

00:08:55.070 --> 00:08:55.590
What?

00:08:56.560 --> 00:09:01.650
I don't know. Maybe I really am.

00:09:01.740 --> 00:09:04.380
I didn't even worry about it
until you brought it up.

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:08.750
But I suppose it's not because of that.

00:09:09.220 --> 00:09:12.020
You went to see the eye specialist, right?

00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:12.910
Yes.

00:09:13.410 --> 00:09:15.220
What did the doctor say?

00:09:16.080 --> 00:09:19.720
He says that if I give up all
reading and sewing entirely

00:09:19.780 --> 00:09:23.370
and any kind of work that strains the eyes,

00:09:23.460 --> 00:09:25.460
and if I'm careful not to cry,

00:09:26.260 --> 00:09:29.040
and if I wear the glasses he's given me

00:09:29.110 --> 00:09:32.690
he thinks my eyes may not get any worse.

00:09:33.610 --> 00:09:39.550
However, if I don't do that, I will be
completely blind within six months.

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:44.850
Just think of it, Anne!
These eyes will see nothing.

00:09:44.940 --> 00:09:45.970
Ah!

00:10:07.060 --> 00:10:07.930
Marilla...

00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:11.580
Marilla, you mustn't think that!

00:10:11.680 --> 00:10:13.730
The doctor has given you hope.

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:18.030
As long as you are careful, you don't
have to worry about becoming blind.

00:10:18.110 --> 00:10:21.250
And if the glasses will cure your
headaches, isn't that good?

00:10:21.950 --> 00:10:24.300
I don't call it much hope.

00:10:24.390 --> 00:10:31.290
What am I to live for if I can't read
or sew or do anything like that?

00:10:32.090 --> 00:10:36.450
If I lose my sight, I might as well be dead.

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:38.240
Marilla...

00:10:38.330 --> 00:10:42.910
And as for crying, I can't
help that when I get lonesome.

00:10:46.410 --> 00:10:51.060
But there, it's no good talking about it.

00:10:53.150 --> 00:10:56.330
If you'll get me a cup of tea,
I'll be thankful.

00:10:57.950 --> 00:11:04.430
I'm just a bit depressed.
There's no need to tell anyone at this time,

00:11:04.530 --> 00:11:08.140
or there will be many people
coming to ask me questions.

00:11:08.230 --> 00:11:11.740
I don't wish to become their
subject of discussion and sympathy.

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:26.330
Marilla, would you like to
go to bed early today?

00:11:26.410 --> 00:11:29.030
Yes. I should do that.

00:11:36.420 --> 00:11:38.210
I'll leave this to you.

00:11:38.290 --> 00:11:40.440
Yes. Goodnight.

00:11:51.620 --> 00:11:52.540
Marilla...

00:12:30.880 --> 00:12:34.070
Anne's heart is as heavy as lead.

00:12:36.550 --> 00:12:42.910
She can't help feeling sad about the
drastic change that has taken place

00:12:42.990 --> 00:12:46.430
since the day she came home
with the Avery scholarship.

00:12:48.430 --> 00:12:55.620
Then she had been full of hope and joy,
and the future had looked rosy with promise.

00:13:09.950 --> 00:13:14.700
Anne feels as if she has lived years since then.

00:13:32.870 --> 00:13:41.020
However, before she goes to bed, there is
a smile on her lips and peace in her heart.

00:13:42.250 --> 00:13:50.330
She has looked her duty courageously
in the face, and finds it a friend,

00:13:50.590 --> 00:13:56.900
as duty ever is when we meet it frankly.

00:14:27.700 --> 00:14:31.740
From the next day, Anne begins
to make several trips.

00:14:32.770 --> 00:14:37.710
Sometimes she even borrows the carriage,
as if she is going somewhere far away.

00:14:43.480 --> 00:14:50.030
On the other hand, Mrs. Rachel Lynde
visits Marilla often to advise her.

00:14:50.120 --> 00:14:55.600
As such, Marilla hasn't noticed
Anne's strange behavior.

00:17:04.390 --> 00:17:08.530
This visitor has been referred by Mrs. Rachel Lynde.

00:17:08.620 --> 00:17:11.280
He's John Sadler from Carmody.

00:17:12.530 --> 00:17:19.970
Anne has no idea that his visit
concerns the fate of Green Gables.

00:17:20.970 --> 00:17:25.080
The house is a little old,
but I'm generally pleased with it.

00:17:25.170 --> 00:17:27.020
Thanks for taking the trouble.

00:17:27.110 --> 00:17:29.150
Well, then. I'll take my leave.

00:17:44.560 --> 00:17:47.240
What did Mr. Sadler want, Marilla?

00:17:59.170 --> 00:18:00.540
What's the matter, Marilla?

00:18:03.180 --> 00:18:07.030
Mr. Sadler heard that you were
going to leave Green Gables,

00:18:07.090 --> 00:18:08.860
and so he came here
saying he'd like to buy it.

00:18:08.950 --> 00:18:11.950
Buy the house?!
He's buying Green Gables?

00:18:17.760 --> 00:18:21.670
Oh, Marilla! You don't intend to sell
Green Gables, do you?

00:18:22.800 --> 00:18:25.300
I don't know what else is to be done, Anne.

00:18:26.170 --> 00:18:28.750
I've thought it over carefully.

00:18:28.840 --> 00:18:35.020
If my eyes were strong, I could stay
here and get along somehow.

00:18:35.510 --> 00:18:38.550
But as it is, I can't.

00:18:38.650 --> 00:18:41.460
I may lose my sight altogether,

00:18:41.880 --> 00:18:46.790
and anyway, I'll not be fit to run things.

00:18:49.460 --> 00:18:55.030
When Abbey Bank declared bankruptcy,
everything was ruined.

00:18:55.800 --> 00:19:00.750
And there are some bills left from last fall.

00:19:01.000 --> 00:19:06.180
It won't bring much. It's small
and the buildings are old.

00:19:06.270 --> 00:19:10.920
But it'll be enough for
me to live on, I reckon.

00:19:11.580 --> 00:19:12.480
Marilla...

00:19:12.710 --> 00:19:17.430
I'm thankful you're provided for
with that scholarship, Anne.

00:19:17.520 --> 00:19:18.370
Marilla...

00:19:18.450 --> 00:19:22.300
I may move to Rachel and board with her.

00:19:22.390 --> 00:19:27.330
I'm sorry you won't have a home
to come to in your vacations, that's all,

00:19:27.430 --> 00:19:32.280
but I suppose you'll manage somehow.

00:19:39.640 --> 00:19:42.990
You mustn't sell Green Gables, Marilla!

00:19:43.080 --> 00:19:45.890
I wish I didn't have to, Anne.

00:19:45.980 --> 00:19:51.190
But you can see for yourself.
I can't stay here alone.

00:19:51.750 --> 00:19:56.070
I'll go crazy worrying and
feeling lonely everyday.

00:19:56.160 --> 00:19:57.700
And, my eyes...

00:19:57.790 --> 00:20:02.280
You won't have to stay here alone, Marilla.
I'll be with you.

00:20:02.360 --> 00:20:04.410
I'm not going to Redmond.

00:20:11.040 --> 00:20:14.370
Not going to Redmond?!
Why, what do you mean?

00:20:14.610 --> 00:20:18.320
Just what I say. I'm not
going to take the scholarship.

00:20:18.410 --> 00:20:21.640
I decided so the night after
you came home from town.

00:20:22.380 --> 00:20:25.940
You surely don't think I could
leave you alone in your trouble, Marilla,

00:20:26.020 --> 00:20:29.240
after all you've done for me.

00:20:29.320 --> 00:20:30.040
But Anne...

00:20:30.190 --> 00:20:30.870
No!

00:20:31.320 --> 00:20:34.120
I've thought it over for a long time.
I've planned everything.

00:20:35.040 --> 00:20:39.540
Mr. Barry wants to rent our field next
year, so you need not worry about that.

00:20:39.630 --> 00:20:41.610
And I'm going to teach.

00:20:41.700 --> 00:20:46.010
I've already submitted applications
to Avonlea and Carmody schools.

00:20:46.370 --> 00:20:51.280
I understand the school here has been promised
to Gilbert Blythe, so it's probably pointless,

00:20:51.540 --> 00:20:53.320
but I can have the Carmody school.

00:20:53.710 --> 00:20:54.700
It may be a little far,

00:20:54.780 --> 00:20:57.630
but I can rent a room there,
and drive myself over in a carriage.

00:20:57.720 --> 00:21:01.700
And I'll read to you and keep you cheered up.

00:21:01.790 --> 00:21:09.110
You won't be bored or lonely.
And we'll be happy here together, you and I.

00:21:10.130 --> 00:21:16.950
But I can't let you sacrifice yourself
so for me. It would be terrible.

00:21:17.040 --> 00:21:19.880
Nonsense! There is no sacrifice!

00:21:20.240 --> 00:21:25.910
Nothing could be worse than giving up
Green Gables. Nothing could hurt me more.

00:21:26.550 --> 00:21:30.360
We must keep the dear old place.

00:21:30.620 --> 00:21:33.000
But your ambitions...

00:21:33.090 --> 00:21:37.420
I'm just as ambitious as ever.
Only, I've changed the object of my ambitions.

00:21:38.330 --> 00:21:42.580
I'm going to be a good teacher,
and I'm going to save your eyesight.

00:21:42.660 --> 00:21:47.380
Besides, I mean to study at home here
and take a little college course all by myself.

00:21:47.530 --> 00:21:51.320
Marilla, I've thought about it this whole week.

00:21:51.410 --> 00:21:56.850
When I left Queen's, my future seemed
to stretch out before me like a straight road.

00:21:57.980 --> 00:22:01.490
But now there is a bend in it.

00:22:01.580 --> 00:22:05.660
I don't know what is waiting beyond that bend.

00:22:05.750 --> 00:22:12.940
Perhaps there is a road of green glory
and soft, checkered light and shadows.

00:22:13.490 --> 00:22:18.900
Beautiful curves and hills and valleys
that I've never seen may be waiting.

00:22:19.850 --> 00:22:23.680
But I'm going to believe that the best is waiting.

00:22:23.770 --> 00:22:30.060
I shall give life here my best,
and I believe it will give its best to me in return.

00:22:31.180 --> 00:22:35.090
I don't feel as if I ought to let you give it up.

00:22:35.180 --> 00:22:39.760
But you can't prevent me. I'm sixteen and a half,

00:22:39.850 --> 00:22:44.870
and 'obstinate as a mule,'
as Mrs. Lynde once told me.

00:22:48.760 --> 00:22:51.850
Oh, Marilla, please don't pity me.

00:22:52.830 --> 00:22:57.350
I don't like to be pitied,
and there is no need for it.

00:22:58.610 --> 00:23:03.390
I'm heart glad over the very thought
of staying at dear Green Gables.

00:23:03.710 --> 00:23:04.640
Anne...

00:23:05.620 --> 00:23:08.930
Nobody could love it as you and I do,

00:23:09.020 --> 00:23:12.860
so we cannot afford to let it go.

00:23:14.080 --> 00:23:16.310
You've convinced me, Anne.

00:23:16.590 --> 00:23:20.340
I feel as if you'd given me new life.

00:23:20.430 --> 00:23:26.360
I guess I ought to stick out
and make you go to college,

00:23:27.070 --> 00:23:33.050
but I know I can't,
so I ain't going to try.

00:23:33.970 --> 00:23:39.890
But Anne, I'll be willing to give up
this house at any time for you.

00:23:41.320 --> 00:23:42.730
Marilla.

00:24:02.500 --> 00:24:05.740
Next on Anne of Green Gables:
Episode 50

00:24:05.870 --> 00:24:09.720
God's in His Heaven,
All's Right with the World

00:24:09.960 --> 00:24:11.330
Please look forward to it!

00:24:14.060 --> 00:24:15.840
The adventures of Tom Sawyer.

00:24:16.010 --> 00:24:18.230
Taking place in the grand nature surrounding Mississippi,

00:24:18.230 --> 00:24:21.710
Tom Sawyer and his friends
experience pleasant adventures.

00:24:21.940 --> 00:24:25.260
A wonderful world, full of dreams and hope.

00:24:25.700 --> 00:24:28.010
The new series 'The Adventures of Tom Sawyer'

00:24:28.010 --> 00:24:29.680
will start this spring!

00:24:29.680 --> 00:24:30.920
Please look forward to it!
